(a) No license issued under this article shall be suspended or revoked except for due cause as defined hereunder, and only after a hearing before the commission of the city upon a prior written notice to the licensee at the address shown on the license of the time, place and purpose of such hearing and a statement of the reason the license would be suspended or revoked. Three days notice prior to the hearing shall be deemed reasonable, but shorter or longer periods of notice shall be authorized as the commission may deem the circumstances justify.
