The following acts, among others, are hereby declared to be and constitute disorderly conduct:
(1) Use of obscene, abusive or profane language;
(2) Making of any threats of violence to or against any other person;
(3) Being drunk, or the extravagant use of alcoholic beverages, drugs or distilled spirits;
(4) Being noisy and disorderly in or upon any street or other public place in the city;
(5) Making any indecent or immoral exposure of the person;
(6) The reckless and dangerous use of firearms or dangerous weapons;
(7) Any noisy or riotous conduct to the disturbance of the public peace and tranquility;
(8) Engaging in, promoting, encouraging, aiding or abetting any fight, riot or noisy and disorderly proceeding on any street or public place, or in any private building or dwelling or on any private premises when persons residing in the vicinity of the private building, dwelling or premises are disturbed; or
(9) Assault and battery upon any person on any street or public place, or in any private building or dwelling or on any private premises when persons residing in the vicinity of the private building, dwelling or premises are disturbed.
(Ord. of 9-10-90, § 2)

